name    hexeditview
prog    hexedit /dd/SYS/motd
# hexedit (HEXPERT 2.4) viewing a file at a vt100, with TERMCAP naming the
# termcap FILE as SYS/login sets it.  The archive's build was linked with
# a curses that read TERMCAP as the entry itself and sent every cursor
# move as ESC [ ; H, so the whole view piled onto the top lines.  Rebuilt
# on 2026-09-26 against LIB/ncurses.l with moria's tcentry.c -- which
# reads SYS/termcap as it stands -- the view draws where it belongs: the
# hex on the left, the same bytes as text on the right.  The arrow keys
# are sent in the keypad form the program switches the terminal to.
rate    0.6
wait    6
snap    view
key     q
wait    3
expect  Status-  Position: 00000000   Mode: View   File: /dd/SYS/motd
expect  57 65 6C 63 6F 6D 65 20 74 6F 20 74 68 65 20 4F     Welcome to the O
